   "notes": [
    "Capo 1, Em shapes (sounds in F minor) — your tutorial shows the capo on fret 1; MJ Music Notes and EliteTarun say the same; ChordZone, UG and IndianGuitarTabs give the same chords without capo (Fm Bbm Eb Ab Db).",
    "Your play-along video (Star Maa upload) plays about 4% fast: ChordU measures it at 96.05 BPM reading F#m, against 92.15 BPM in F minor for the film audio (96.05 ÷ 92.15 = 1.042 ≈ PAL 25/24). Chordify also flags it as off-standard tuning (~433 Hz). With that video, capo 1 sounds ~70 cents flat; use capo 2 (same shapes) and set the tuner to A4 = 432. With the film audio / your own MP3: capo 1, A4 = 440, ~92 BPM.",
    "BPM 96 matches the play-along video; the song itself is ~92 (ChordU on the film audio; ChordZone says 90).",
    "Strumming: your tutorial explains its pattern out loud (0:31–0:51) with no on-screen text, so it is not in here yet — tell me the pattern and it becomes Pattern 4.",
    "Bar counts come from the chord sheets (one chord per bar, ~2 bars per lyric line), not from the recording — run pipeline/songbook_pipeline.py on your MP3 to align them."
